# `core.autocrlf` is true on this machine, and CRLF is the right thing for the
# C++ and the PowerShell -- they are only ever read by tools that do not care.
#
# A script with a shebang IS different: a CRLF after `#!/usr/bin/env python3`
# makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named `python3\r`, and the
# error it gives says nothing useful. Force those to LF at the source.
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
